# Case of the Gorgon's Kiss: "destroy up to one target creature that was dealt damage this turn" (CR 115.1, 601.2c, 701.8a) "up to one" lets the controller choose no target even when a legal one exists. On turn 3 Bot1's Memnite
# attacks and Bot2 blocks it with an Ornithopter, which is dealt 1 damage and survives. Bot1 casts the Case and declines to target; the damaged Ornithopter stays. The other scenario, which does choose it, is the positive control.

[Bot1 Deck]
Memnite
Mox Jet
Case of the Gorgon's Kiss
Island x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Ornithopter
Mountain x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Memnite.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot2.Pass
[T3 Bot1.DeclareAttackers]
Bot1.Attack(Memnite > Bot2)
Bot2.Block(Ornithopter > Memnite)
[T3 Bot1.Main2]
? Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Damage = 1
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Case of the Gorgon's Kiss.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Target()
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass

[Expect]
Bot2.Battlefield = Ornithopter
Bot2.Graveyard.Count = 0
Bot1.Battlefield = Case of the Gorgon's Kiss; Memnite; Mox Jet
